{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.UnitModulusEigenvalue","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.UnitModulusEigenvalue","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.Notation","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.Trace","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Int.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Group.Units.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.GroupWithZero.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":11,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.borromean_trace_standard","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.borromean_trace_standard","kind":"theorem","line":146,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/UnitModulusEigenvalue.lean#L146-L159","doc":"**Borromean trace on `V_{(2,1)}`.**\n`χ_{(2,1)}((σ₁σ₂⁻¹)³) = −(q⁴−q²+1)(q⁸−2q⁶−2q²+1)/q⁶`.\nAt `q = 1` this is `2`, so the eigenvalues are near `+1`, not `−1`. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:unit-modulus-eigenvalue","label":"prop:unit-modulus-eigenvalue","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/unit-modulus-eigenvalue.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.unitMod_s1_mul_s2inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.unitMod_s1_mul_s2inv","kind":"theorem","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/UnitModulusEigenvalue.lean#L139-L144","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.unitModBor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.unitModBor","kind":"def","line":134,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/UnitModulusEigenvalue.lean#L134-L137","doc":"`σ₁σ₂⁻¹` in the model. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.unitMod_trace_s1s2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.unitMod_trace_s1s2","kind":"theorem","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/UnitModulusEigenvalue.lean#L128-L132","doc":"`χ_{(2,1)}(σ₁σ₂) = −1` for every `q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.unitMod_braid","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.unitMod_braid","kind":"theorem","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/UnitModulusEigenvalue.lean#L121-L126","doc":"The braid relation `σ₁σ₂σ₁ = σ₂σ₁σ₂` holds in the model. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.unitMod_s2_mul_s2inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.unitMod_s2_mul_s2inv","kind":"theorem","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/UnitModulusEigenvalue.lean#L115-L119","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.unitModS2inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.unitModS2inv","kind":"def","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/UnitModulusEigenvalue.lean#L111-L113","doc":"`σ₂⁻¹ = σ₂ − h`, from the Hecke relation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.unitModS2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.unitModS2","kind":"def","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/UnitModulusEigenvalue.lean#L106-L109","doc":"`σ₂` on `V_{(2,1)}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.unitModS1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.unitModS1","kind":"def","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/UnitModulusEigenvalue.lean#L103-L104","doc":"`σ₁` on `V_{(2,1)}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.even_braid_det_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.even_braid_det_one","kind":"theorem","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/UnitModulusEigenvalue.lean#L84-L90","doc":"A product of an even number `2k` of Hecke generators on `V_{(2,1)}`\nhas determinant `(−1)^{2k} = 1` (each generator contributes `−1`).\nTogether with `|tr| ≤ 2` this is the unit-circle condition\n`λ₁λ₂ = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.hecke_generator_det_neg_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.hecke_generator_det_neg_one","kind":"theorem","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/UnitModulusEigenvalue.lean#L68-L80","doc":"The Hecke relation `σ² = h·σ + 1` forces `det(σ) = −1` on every\n2-dimensional Wedderburn block: the eigenvalues of `σ` are `q` and\n`−q⁻¹` (roots of `x² − h·x − 1`), with product `q·(−q⁻¹) = −1`.\n\n§7c: a **units** identity over a plain `CommRing` — the second\neigenvalue is only defined when `q` is invertible, so `q` is carried as\n`q : Rˣ` and the inverse is `Units.inv`. Over a field this is exactly\nthe old `q ≠ 0`; unlike the field version it also applies over\n`ℤ[q, q⁻¹]`, where `q` is a unit but no division is available. ","signatureChunk":0}]}